      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In its heyday, Tasley boasted the first electric power plant, first paved road, and first self‑organized volunteer fire company in the county.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tasley%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Passenger trains stopped running in 1958, and the Route 13 bypass of the mid‑1960s stripped Tasley of its commercial heart.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
